        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">soil nutrient management</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Integrated nutrient management refers to the maintenance of soil fertility and of plant nutrient supply at an optimum level for sustaining the desired productivity through optimization of the benefits from all possible sources of organic, inorganic and biological components in an integrated manner.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Integrated nutrient management refers to the maintenance of soil fertility and of plant nutrient supply at an optimum level for sustaining the desired productivity through optimization of the benefits from all possible sources of organic, inorganic and biological components in an integrated manner.</schema:description>
