        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">sequential cropping</skos:altLabel>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">Crop rotation on arable land is the practice of alternating crops grown on a specific field in a planned pattern or sequence in successive crop years so that crops of the same species are not grown without interruption on the same field. In a rotation the crops are normally changed annually, but they can also be multi-annual.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">Crop rotation on arable land is the practice of alternating crops grown on a specific field in a planned pattern or sequence in successive crop years so that crops of the same species are not grown without interruption on the same field. In a rotation the crops are normally changed annually, but they can also be multi-annual.</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


