        <cpr:P3 rdf:resource="https://climatepolicyradar.wikibase.cloud/entity/Q994"/>
        <cpr:P7 xml:lang="en">A drought is an extended period of abnormally dry weather with significantly reduced precipitation over a large area lasting more than a month. It results in below-average moisture, impacting natural systems and economic sectors. Droughts can be meteorological, agricultural, ecological, or hydrological, and often affect multiple areas of the Earth system simultaneously or sequentially.</cpr:P7>
        <schema:description xml:lang="en">A drought is an extended period of unusually dry weather marked by a significant and sustained lack of precipitation, falling below a specific threshold over a large area for more than a month</schema:description>
    </owl:Class>
    


