        <schema:description xml:lang="en">A floating building is a building unit with a flotation system at its base, to allow it to float on water. It is common to define such a building as being &quot;permanently moored&quot; and not usable in navigation. Floating buildings have environmental benefits such as unsusceptibility to changes in sea level.</schema:description>
